# 022 - len of a non-Str is a Type error. error.rs ships no builtin-specific
# constructor, and §4 forbids a format! at the call site, so the only legal
# wording available is unary_type_mismatch(line, "len", "Str", got) - the same
# constructor unary - uses (033). Bead .39 proposed "len expects Str, found Int"
# instead, which no constructor produces; see the spec-gap bead filed with this
# corpus.
--- source
print len(5);
--- expect
error: Type at line 1: len expects a Str operand, got Int
